1
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:03,500
Here you go, Pheebs.

2
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:06,330
Who wants one of my special home-baked brownies?

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,580
I'll have one.

4
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:12,170
- That's okay.     - I'm not having one.

5
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,880
No, no. It's just my tooth.

6
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,970
- All right.     - I'll have one.

7
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,680
So you need a dentist? I've got a good one.

8
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:25,100
Thanks. I have a good one too. I just can't see him.

9
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:28,190
See, that is the problem with invisible dentists.

10
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:31,280
Why can't you go to him?

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:36,360
Because every time I go to the dentist, somebody dies.

12
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:40,490
That's so weird. Every time I go to the dentist...

13
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,870
...I look down the hygienist's blouse.

14
00:00:43,910 --> 00:00:46,290
Phoebe, what, um?

15
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:47,540
What?

16
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:49,290
First, it was my Aunt Mary.

17
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:52,090
And then there was, um, John, my mailman.

18
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,880
And then my cowboy friend, Albino Bob.

19
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:58,300
Ahem. And all these people actually died?

20
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:00,680
Yes. While I was in the chair.

21
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:04,020
That's why I take care of my teeth. It's not about oral hygiene.

22
00:01:04,270 --> 00:01:06,310
I floss to save lives.

23
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:09,150
Come on, you didn't kill anybody.

24
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:13,070
These people just happened to die when you went to the dentist.

25
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,740
It's just a coincidence.

26
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:17,740
Tell that to them. Oh, you can't! They're dead!

27
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:28,800
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

28
00:01:29,370 --> 00:01:33,540
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

29
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:38,260
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

30
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,820
# When it hasn't been your day, #

31
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:43,820
# your week, your month, or even your year #

32
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:47,780
# but I'll be there for you #

33
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,610
# When the rain starts to pour #

34
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:52,730
# I'll be there for you #

35
00:01:52,730 --> 00:01:54,570
# Like I've been there before #

36
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:57,580
# I'll be there for you #

37
00:01:57,580 --> 00:02:01,240
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

38
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:08,030

39
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:09,920
Thanks, Gunther.

40
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,380
- Hi.     - Hey.

41
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:13,000
Um, can I get a napkin too?

42
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:15,840
Oh, like you don't already have everything.

43
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:24,850
You're in pain. Would you just go to the dentist? Just go.

44
00:02:25,010 --> 00:02:27,140
Fine. But if you're my next victim...

45
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:30,640
...don't come back as a poltergeist who sucks me into the TV set.

46
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:32,480
I promise.

47
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:34,570
Although, don't feel like you can't visit.

48
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,700
Hey, is Chandler here?

49
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:42,450
No. No, he's not.

50
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:48,580
You guys, Joey just saw Janice kissing her ex-husband.

51
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:50,000
What?

52
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:53,210
What are you gonna do? How are you gonna tell Chandler?

53
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:56,630
I was thinking about that. I think the best way would be...

54
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,840
...to not.

55
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:02,010
Joey, if you know about this, you have to tell him.

56
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:04,470
It'll kill him. It'll just kill him.

57
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:07,510
Wait till I go to the dentist. Maybe I'll kill him.

58
00:03:13,190 --> 00:03:18,110
Ugly Naked Guy's using a hammock. It's like a Play-Doh fat factory.

59
00:03:19,110 --> 00:03:21,200
I'm going to the dentist. So listen...

60
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:25,620
...just be on the lookout for anything that you could fall into...

61
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:28,450
...or that can fall on you...

62
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:30,000
...or...

63
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,540
All right, just look out!

64
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,540
Okay? And, um, I also just want to...

65
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,960
I just want to tell you all that, um...

66
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,430
I have a problem. I have to go into work for a few hours.

67
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,970
Some kids messed up the Homo sapien display.

68
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:51,560
What did they do?

69
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:54,850
They painted over the word "sapien," for one thing.

70
00:03:55,730 --> 00:04:00,610
Then they rearranged the figures. Let's just leave it at that.

71
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:02,570
Do you want me to watch Ben for you?

72
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,530
Yes, that's what I was gonna ask. Thank you.

73
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:07,530
Woah, wait, hello! Heh, what about me?

74
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:11,120
You. You want to watch Ben?

75
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:17,960
That would be great! I just asked Monica...

76
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:20,420
...because I know how empty her life is.

77
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:27,510
- Hey, Ross? I got a science question.     - Yeah. Mm-hm.

78
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:33,480
If the Homo sapiens were, in fact, "homo" sapiens...

79
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:36,400
...is that why they're extinct?

80
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:43,440
Joey, Homo sapiens are people.

81
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:44,950
Hey, I'm not judging.

82
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:50,160
Look, Benny! Spoon!

83
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,450
Spoon!

84
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:56,790
Come on. All right, you know what? I think he's bored.

85
00:04:57,210 --> 00:04:59,500
Here. You wanna play the airplane game?

86
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:01,630
You wanna show Rachel? Come here.

87
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,880
You wanna do something fun? Okay.

88
00:05:15,230 --> 00:05:18,350
You're so brave. You're so brave! Yes, you are.

89
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,440
- You're so brave.     - You're okay.

90
00:05:20,610 --> 00:05:22,860
He's fine. Let's just put him down.

91
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:25,940
Come here, babe. Yes, you're such a good boy.

92
00:05:26,110 --> 00:05:30,370
How could you do that to him? Ross trusted me! What's he gonna say?

93
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:32,580
Nothing, because we're not telling him.

94
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:33,910
- We're not?     - No.

95
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:36,080
- All right, I like that.     - Okay.

96
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:39,170
So we're okay. We're okay, aren't we?

97
00:05:39,330 --> 00:05:41,040
No, we're not okay. There's a bump.

98
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:42,920
- There's a bump.     - What bump?

99
00:05:43,090 --> 00:05:45,630
Oh, my God! Well, push it in! Push it in!

100
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:48,590
I can not push it in!

101
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:51,550
- Okay, we're gonna need a distraction.     - Okay.

102
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,970
- That's it.     - Okay.

103
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,310
- I got it!     - Okay.

104
00:05:54,470 --> 00:05:56,180
- The second Ross walks in...     - Yeah.

105
00:05:56,350 --> 00:05:59,640
...take him to your bedroom and do whatever you do that makes him go:

106
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:04,780
Or...

107
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,110
...we could put a hat on his head.

108
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:13,120
A hat! Yes! We need a hat! Where are we gonna find a tiny little hat?

109
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,950
Oh, oh, oh! I'll get Rainy Day Bear!

110
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:17,450
Because he'll know what to do?

111
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:19,370
Oh, my God. You're a genius!

112
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:21,460
Oh, God. It's kind of sewn on.

113
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:23,090
- Give it. Give it.     - Okay.

114
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:30,800
Agh, it's just like a bloodbath in here today!

115
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:38,430
Hey, hold on a second. Hold on a second.

116
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,400
Do you think these pearls are nice?

117
00:06:42,690 --> 00:06:44,440
I'd prefer a mountain bike.

118
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:48,990
Janice's birthday's coming. I wanna get her something special.

119
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:53,200
- Come in here with me.     - Woah, woah, whoa, wait. Woah.

120
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:57,660
You wanna get her something special? Get her flowers.

121
00:06:57,830 --> 00:07:00,580
Get her candy. Get her gum. Girls love gum.

122
00:07:01,290 --> 00:07:04,750
That's a good idea. "Dear Janice: Have a Hubba-Bubba birthday."

123
00:07:06,130 --> 00:07:08,340
I'd like to get her something serious.

124
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:11,090
Oh, you want something serious.

125
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:14,590
You know what you should do? You should get her one of those, um...

126
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,220
...barium enemas.

127
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:20,270
Those are dead serious.

128
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:25,110
Look, I'm gonna go in here. And you don't buy me anything, ever!

129
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:27,940
You can't! You can't. You can't buy her pearls.

130
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:30,530
You just can't, you can't, you can't!

131
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,450
Why not?

132
00:07:33,990 --> 00:07:36,280
Oh, God. Uh, okay.

133
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:38,950
Here's the thing. Ahem.

134
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:41,660
This is the thing. Okay, the thing is...

135
00:07:41,830 --> 00:07:42,960
- What is the thing?     - Okay.

136
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:47,920
I went down to the Mattress King's showroom...

137
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:51,010
...and I saw Janice kissing her ex-husband.

138
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:54,300
What?

139
00:07:54,470 --> 00:07:56,090
They were in his office.

140
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:02,310
Well, she... She wouldn't do that. She's with me.

141
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,140
I'm telling you, I saw it.

142
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:06,230
Well, you're wrong. Okay? You're wrong.

143
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:08,060
I'm not wrong.

144
00:08:08,230 --> 00:08:10,440
I wish I was.

145
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,950
I'm sorry.

146
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:20,370
Bet that barium enema doesn't sound so bad now, huh?

147
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:28,040
It makes more sense as an ensemble. And it takes the focus off the hat.

148
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:31,960
Oh! You're alive! You're alive!

149
00:08:33,170 --> 00:08:35,800
See? I promised you no one would die, didn't I?

150
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:39,510
We'll see about that. Can I use your phone to call everyone I know?

151
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:42,470
Sure. We have no money. Go ahead.

152
00:08:43,770 --> 00:08:46,980
Hey, you're not dead! Okay, see you.

153
00:08:49,190 --> 00:08:50,730
Monica.

154
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:53,570
Oh, my God! He just said my name!

155
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:55,570
- Did you hear that?     - Yeah.

156
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:58,160
Monica bang!

157
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,790
Ahem. Okay, I heard that.

158
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,290
Did he just say, "Monica bang"?

159
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:09,130
Oh, my God! He's gonna rat me out!

160
00:09:09,790 --> 00:09:12,420
Monica bang!

161
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:16,340
Sweetie, you need to stop saying that now.

162
00:09:16,510 --> 00:09:19,090
It's no big deal. It's not even worth mentioning.

163
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,350
You see? We all do it all the time.

164
00:09:21,510 --> 00:09:22,640
See? Watch this.

165
00:09:22,810 --> 00:09:24,770
Ben, Ben, Ben. Ow.

166
00:09:24,930 --> 00:09:27,640
Monica bang! Everybody bang!

167
00:09:27,810 --> 00:09:29,150
Ben bang!

168
00:09:29,310 --> 00:09:30,940
Rachel bang!

169
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:33,110
Bang, Rachel! Bang!

170
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:36,150
- Oh, isn't it fun?     - Look at that! Look at that!

171
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:38,200
We all do it!

172
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,660
- Okay, I'm stopping now.     - Are you okay?

173
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:44,910
Oh, yeah. You know, if it's not a headboard, it's just not worth it.

174
00:09:56,010 --> 00:09:58,090
How's my Bing-a-ling?

175
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:03,010
I don't know.

176
00:10:03,810 --> 00:10:05,220
You tell me.

177
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:09,350
Anything you, uh, want to tell me?

178
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,270
Because if you, uh... You should...

179
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,570
You would tell me.

180
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:18,030
Why are your eyes so wide?

181
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:20,490
You tell me.

182
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:23,490
Maybe it's because I was just fooling around with my ex.

183
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:26,120
Oh, no. No, no, no. That was you!

184
00:10:26,290 --> 00:10:27,660
Oh, my God!

185
00:10:27,830 --> 00:10:29,660
- All right!     - How did you know?

186
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:32,000
Joey told me. He saw you two kissing.

187
00:10:32,170 --> 00:10:33,710
In the park?

188
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:37,670
No. In his office. How many kisses were there?

189
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,590
- Just those two!     - Wh...? Why? Why?

190
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,550
Why was there kissing? There should be no kissing!

191
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:46,470
Oh, I'm sorry, honey. I'm so, so...

192
00:10:47,850 --> 00:10:49,430
I'm so, so sorry. I just...

193
00:10:51,810 --> 00:10:54,560
What happened was I... I can't breathe.

194
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:58,490
Can you get me a bag or something? Aah.

195
00:10:58,650 --> 00:11:00,150
Here. Here.

196
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,400
There.

197
00:11:04,910 --> 00:11:07,160
- It's the receipt.     - I'll take it.

198
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:10,460
Look, I've got to know.

199
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:14,750
Are you finished with me?

200
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,380
Are you finished with him?

201
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:25,760
Do you still love him?

202
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:30,140
Do you still love me?

203
00:11:32,270 --> 00:11:33,480
All right, look...

204
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:37,230
...I'm gonna need an actual answer here, okay?

205
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,320
So which is it?

206
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:42,030
Him or me?

207
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:53,250
I don't know.

208
00:11:55,210 --> 00:11:58,920
Okay, if you're alive, you answer your phone!

209
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:07,760
Ben, I won't tell your daddy that you had ice cream before dinner...

210
00:12:07,930 --> 00:12:11,770
...if you won't tell him about our little bonking incident.

211
00:12:11,930 --> 00:12:15,400
Number one, I don't think Ben understands the concept of bribery.

212
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:17,270
And number two, I...

213
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,480
What?

214
00:12:20,650 --> 00:12:23,110
You said "number two."

215
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,410
I also said "number one."

216
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,160
Ha-ha-ha, I know.

217
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:33,330
- Hey, everyone!     - Hi!

218
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,500
How's my little boy?

219
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:37,670
He's perfect. Aren't you, Ben?

220
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,550
- He's never been better.     - What did you do, take him whaling?

221
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,050
Monica.

222
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:49,600
Oh, my God! He just said your name! That's great! Good job, Ben!

223
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:52,020
Monica bang!

224
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,680
Ha-ha-ha. That's right.

225
00:12:53,850 --> 00:12:56,770
That's what I'd sound like if I exploded.

226
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:01,400
Woo-hoo! The curse is broken! I called everybody I know...

227
00:13:01,570 --> 00:13:03,440
...and everyone is alive!

228
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:07,610
What?

229
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:12,040
Ugly Naked Guy looks awfully still.

230
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:19,420
Oh, my God, I killed another one!

231
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:23,670
The curse is getting stronger too, to bring down something that big.

232
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:26,090
Maybe he's just taking a nap.

233
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:28,800
I'm telling you, he hasn't moved since this morning.

234
00:13:28,970 --> 00:13:30,470
We should call somebody.

235
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:33,890
Tell them the naked guy we stare at isn't moving?

236
00:13:34,060 --> 00:13:36,390
We've got to find out if he's alive.

237
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:39,020
How are we gonna do that? There's no way.

238
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:40,980
Well, there is one way.

239
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:44,070
His window's open. I say...

240
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,740
...we poke him.

241
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:50,990
Hey!

242
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,740
You know how we, uh, save all those chopsticks...

243
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:56,370
...for no reason when we get Chinese food?

244
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:57,660
Yeah?

245
00:13:57,830 --> 00:14:00,250
Well, now we got a reason.

246
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:02,210
What?

247
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:05,300
Well, we're fashioning a very long poking device.

248
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,760
All right.

249
00:14:11,430 --> 00:14:13,890
Hey, uh, what's the matter?

250
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,020
I talked to Janice.

251
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:21,270
Oh, my God. Is she going back to him?

252
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:23,110
She doesn't know.

253
00:14:23,270 --> 00:14:24,770
Says she loves us both.

254
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:29,450
I woke up this morning, I was in love.

255
00:14:29,610 --> 00:14:31,410
I was happy!

